course: dictionary
lesson: 7745
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have many meanings, and context tells you which one you need. «She used the hole punch to make two neat holes in the paper.» Hole punch is a tool here, because the holes and the paper are the clues. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Punch as a hit is a word you need to understand, but hitting someone is never OK. If someone hurts you or threatens to, tell an adult straight away. In a story, the clues show what kind of punch is meant: a fist, a bruise, or a fight.
explain: Some meanings are fixed phrases. A «punch line» is the funny end of a joke. To «pack a punch» means to have a lot of strength or force. If you are not sure, read the words around the phrase, and then check a dictionary.
fact: Punch can mean to hit hard with a closed fist. Hitting someone is never OK; tell an adult.
fact: Punch can mean to make a hole in something with a tool, such as a hole punch for paper.
fact: Punch can be a sweet drink made from fruit juices, served from a big bowl at parties.
fact: Punch can mean to press keys or buttons, as in «punch in a number».
fact: Early programs were punched into cards: «people punched holes into cards, each hole meaning a number or an instruction.»
exercise: «She used the hole punch to make two neat holes in the paper.» What is a hole punch? | A sweet drink | A hard hit with a closed fist | *A tool for making holes in paper | A joke's funny end
exercise: At the party, a big bowl held fruit punch. What is punch here? | *A sweet drink made from fruit juices | A hard hit with the fist | A tool for making holes | To press buttons
exercise: «The comedian's joke had a great punch line.» What does punch line mean? | A hard hit at the end of a fight | A hole in the paper | *The funny end of a joke | A bowl for drinks
test: «Early programs were not typed on screens: people punched holes into cards.» What does punched mean here? | To drink a bowl of punch | To hit hard with a fist | *To make holes in something with a tool | To laugh at a joke
test: The recipe says, «mix 2 litres of juice with 1 litre of lemonade» to make punch. What is punch in this recipe? | Strength in a speech | A hard hit | To press buttons on a machine | *A sweet drink
exam: «The speech had real punch.» What does punch mean in this sentence? | To hit someone with a closed fist | *Strength and force that makes the idea hit home | To make a hole in paper with a tool | A bowl of fruit drink
